{
  "$comment": "Community-maintained catalog of AI agents, MCP servers, and agent harnesses. Public domain (CC0) — see catalog/LICENSE. Entries tag matching components as known agents; components that structured parsing could not identify are also named from the catalog. Two match styles: `match` (v1) matches when every non-null field matches the component (pathContains is a case-insensitive substring test on the resolved path; bundleId and nameExact are exact, case-insensitive). `detect` (v2) lists exact identifiers, each scoped to its install method (cliNames only match CLIs found on PATH, npmPackages only npm packages, ...); any one matching is a match. A trailing * on an npm name is a prefix match. `signing.teamIds` are the Apple Developer team IDs the agent ships under; leave empty until verified (run `agent-inventory catalog suggest` on a Mac that has the agent, and cite the evidence). `dataPaths` list where the agent keeps transcripts, instructions, logins and models; the scanner only measures them (size, file count, last change) and never reads contents. Entries never guess: no match means the component stays as it was.",
